csv - Unix-style commands for CSV files
=======================================

csv is a collection of Unix-style utilities for working with CSV files
on a row basis rather than a line basis. This properly handles CSV files
with quoted fields that may contain newlines or commas.

Commands
--------

  csv head [-N|+N] [-a] [file]        Show first N data rows (default: 10)
                                      +N shows all but last N rows
  csv tail [-N|+N] [-a] [file]        Show last N data rows (default: 10)
                                      +N starts from row N to end
  csv wc [-l] [-w] [-c] [-a] [file]   Count rows, columns, and bytes
  csv cut [-a] [-f file] field...     Select specific columns by name
  csv pick [-a] [-f file] row...      Select specific rows by number
  csv grep [-a] [-v] [-f file] regex [field...]
                                      Select rows matching a regex
  csv sort [-a] [-n] [-r] [-f file] [field...]
                                      Sort rows by field values

Options
-------

  -a, --add-header    Include header row (and comments) in output
  -f <file>           Specify input file (for cut, pick, grep, sort)
  -v, --invert        Invert match (for grep)
  -n, --numeric       Numeric sort (for sort)
  -r, --reverse       Reverse/descending order (for sort)
  -l                  Count rows only (wc)
  -w                  Count columns only (wc)
  -c                  Count bytes only (wc)
  -N                  Number of rows (head/tail)
  +N                  POSIX-style offset (head/tail)

When no file is specified, reads from standard input.

Examples
--------

  csv head -5 data.csv              First 5 data rows
  csv head -5 -a data.csv           First 5 rows with header
  csv tail +3 data.csv              Skip first 2 rows, show rest
  csv head +5 data.csv              All but last 5 rows
  csv wc data.csv                   Count rows, columns, bytes
  csv wc -l data.csv                Count data rows only
  csv cut -f data.csv name email    Select name and email columns
  csv cut -a -f data.csv name       Same, with header included
  csv pick -f data.csv 1 3 5        Select rows 1, 3, and 5
  csv pick -a -f data.csv 1 3 5     Same, with header
  cat data.csv | csv pick 2 4       Select rows from stdin
  csv grep -f data.csv "^A" name    Rows where name starts with A
  csv grep -a -f data.csv "NY" city Same, with header
  csv grep -v -f data.csv "test" x  Rows where x doesn't match "test"
  csv grep -f data.csv "error"      Search all fields for "error"
  csv grep -f data.csv "A" name city  Search in name and city fields
  csv sort -f data.csv name         Sort alphabetically by name
  csv sort -n -f data.csv age       Sort numerically by age
  csv sort -a -n -r -f data.csv age Sort descending with header
  csv sort -f data.csv city name    Sort by city, then by name
  csv sort -f data.csv              Sort by all fields in order

Installation
------------

  sudo make install                 Install to /usr/local
  make install prefix=$HOME/.local  Install to home directory

Requirements: Python 3.6 or later (uses only standard library)

